<title>CHILE: Chile trade deficit at $201 mln in December.</title>
<headline>Chile trade deficit at $201 mln in December.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile posted a $201.2 million trade deficit in December, versus a surplus of $64.5 million in the same month last year, the Central Bank reported.</p>
<p>The trade gap, roughly in line with monthly deficits in the second half of this year, was on imports of $1.44 billion and exports of $1.24 billion, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>Details on the figures, as well as annual figures, were due to be released later.</p>
<p>((--Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-6-699-5595 x211))</p>
